{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable basis\nThis reconciler-test cohort contains 45 confirmed bloated prose blocks across exactly 10 file-impact paths. Condense repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, and obsolete history while retaining current non-obvious contracts.\n\nThe inventory and before-citations are pinned to `origin/main@ba24f8734c922c9867645f20df35349bed885419`. All 10 paths moved under `tests/unit/reconciler/apply` and exist on current `origin/main`. Revalidated the 45 targeted docstring/comment anchors there; the create-path test is now named `test_create_path_comment_drop_promotes_to_error`. Use ba24f8734c922c9867645f20df35349bed885419 as the immutable before side and filter grouped-commit checks to this leaf's 10 paths.\n\n## Editing boundary and semantic guard\nEdit only allowlisted comments/docstrings plus adjacent blank lines. Executable statements, assertions, runtime strings, directives, and unlisted prose stay unchanged. Rewrite stale RED/pre-fix language as current contracts.\n\nFor every path, parse immutable and final source with `ast.parse(source, type_comments=True)`; recursively strip only a leading `Expr(Constant(str))` from each `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, and `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require exact `ast.dump(..., include_attributes=False)` equality. A tokenizer guard separately preserves directive text/attachment; runtime strings remain AST-identical.\n\n## Scope — 45 editable blocks\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_fail_loud_comment_errors.py` (2) — module and test_create_path_comment_drop_promotes_to_error docstrings. Preserve warn-first default, flag-gated promotion, partial comment loss, and same-kind silent-no-op canaries.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_fail_loud_exit_and_preflight.py` (1) — module docstring beginning “beer-datum-bark…”. Preserve nonzero exit on recorded mutation failures, clean-pass zero exit, and nonfatal preflight warnings.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_handler_404_isolation.py` (3) — module and both test docstrings. Preserve per-mutation 404 isolation with batch continuation and propagation of non-404 HTTP failures.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_impossible_links_cicada.py` (12) — module and `store`; ten test docstrings anchored by structural refusal, one-attempt skip, durable store, reopen, endpoint comment, transient failure, warning cadence, third-ticket cycle, ancestor status, and commit-back staging. Preserve structural-only classification, precise invalidation, retry, persistence, and staging.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_backfill.py` (3) — module; test_backfill_never_overwrites_proven_evidence; and test_lost_update_backfill_and_snapshot_records_both_survive docstrings. Preserve absence-only grandfathering, no downgrade, snapshot upgrade, ordering on one shared store, and lost-update protection.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_snapshot.py` (8) — module docstring; docstrings of test_unobserved_issue_confirms_nothing, test_authoritative_empty_confirms_nothing_and_unconfirms_nothing, test_get_or_empty_idiom_would_break_the_trichotomy, test_inward_blocks_is_recorded_as_depends_on, test_reconfirmation_is_idempotent_and_does_not_rewrite, test_confirmation_failure_does_not_break_the_pass, and test_two_passes_over_unchanged_snapshot_do_not_rewrite_the_sidecar. Preserve absent/empty/present snapshot trichotomy, link direction, idempotence, fail-open persistence, and no sidecar rewrite.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_peer_confirmations_store.py` (5) — module and _LinkClient docstrings; docstrings of test_relation_scoped_key_does_not_confirm_a_sibling_relation, test_store_survives_snapshot_compaction_of_the_ticket_log, and test_commit_only_peer_confirmations_is_staged_and_committed. Preserve relation-scoped durable keys, protocol-shaped transport, compaction survival, and confirmation-only commit staging.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_sync_only_scalar_update_dispatch_heldout.py` (3) — module docstring; comments beginning “subprocess_env() (not dict(os.environ))…” and “The reconciler unit-test conftests inject…”. Preserve live --only and legacy-filter dispatch parity, secret-safe subprocess repr, and removal of inherited sandbox overrides.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_synced_fields_reporting_e6e9.py` (6) — module docstring; docstrings of test_a_completed_write_reports_every_field_it_sent, test_an_unreachable_transition_reports_nothing, test_a_400_illegal_transition_comment_fallback_reports_nothing, test_a_parent_only_mutation_reports_nothing, and test_the_handler_records_nothing_for_a_soft_failed_mutation. Preserve reporting only confirmed scalar writes across success, transition, 400-comment fallback, 404, parent-only, and handler aggregation paths.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_transition_error_soft_fail.py` (2) — module and test_transition_runtime_error_soft_fails_batch_continues docstrings. Preserve bare transition RuntimeError isolation, continued batch execution, and precise failure manifest recording.\n\n## Consumers and protected directives\nPytest directly collects every impacted module; `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` is the deterministic prose-policy consumer. No targeted `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or doctest consumer was found. Seventeen directives: 2 union-attr ignores in fail-loud comments; 1 union-attr + 5 attr-defined in fail-loud exit; 1 arg-type in handler-404; 1 pragma + 3 E402 noqas + 1 arg-type in synced-fields; 3 union-attr in transition soft-fail. Preserve each complete directive token and its attached executable statement exactly.\n\n## Independent review receipt\nA reviewer who did not author the prose change must post exactly 45 leaf-linked TSV rows, one per edited block:\n`path<TAB>anchor/kind<TAB>before-citation<TAB>after-citation<TAB>preserved-contract-or-consumer<TAB>before-words<TAB>after-words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer-session`\n\nBoth verdicts are `PASS`, citations use full SHAs, and every after count is lower. Missing, duplicate, or extra rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly 45 allowlisted blocks change.\n- [ ] Every changed block is shorter.\n- [ ] Every changed block states only current rationale or constraints.\n- [ ] Every unlisted prose block is byte-identical.\n- [ ] `semantic` exits 0.\n- [ ] `directives` exits 0.\n- [ ] `paths` exits 0 for exactly 10 file-impact paths.\n- [ ] `diff` exits 0.\n- [ ] `hygiene` exits 0.\n- [ ] `focused` exits 0.\n- [ ] Untimed `full` exits 0.\n- [ ] The non-author TSV has exactly 45 rows.\n- [ ] TSV stable IDs are unique.\n- [ ] Every row cites the full immutable-base SHA.\n- [ ] Every row cites the full final SHA.\n- [ ] Every row records `after_words < before_words`.\n- [ ] Every row records `semantic-preservation=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every row records `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every row names a non-author reviewer session.\n\n## Verification\nRun all seven structured commands: `semantic`, `directives`, `paths`, `diff`, `hygiene`, `focused`, and `full`. Executable guards prove behavior/directive/path preservation; the TSV decides each block’s semantic preservation and bloat removal."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792731870526216383,"uuid":"2e1a8d7a-6a18-42c8-acd5-fef71f235419"}